TOOTH-NARROWING LEMMA (to prove): if core P is safe at level mu on an interval around t0=a/q,
and outlier w is ALIGNED (q | w, so w*m has a tooth at t0), then M(P u {w*m}) is nondecreasing
in m and -> M(P). Mechanism: ||w*m*t|| ~ w*m*|t-t0| near t0 (tooth half-width mu/(w*m) -> 0);
P-safe interval around t0 has width ~ (M(P)-mu)/slope; family safe at mu iff mu/(w*m) < that width,
so achievable mu increases to M(P) as m grows. This proves Step 1 for aligned lcm-carriers.
